      <div type="clause" n="35.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 35.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="35.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="104" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif mon to þam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.11-2"/> men feoh geteme, ðe his ǽr oðswaren<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.12-2"/> hæfde ⁊ eft oðswerian<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.13"/> wille, oðswerige<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.14"/> be ðam wite ⁊ be ðæs feos weorðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.15"/>; gif he oðswerian nylle, gebete þone mænan að<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.16"/> twybote.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="35.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="104" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.4"/> to þæm<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.8"/> men feoh<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.9"/> geteme<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.10"/>, þe his ǽr oþsworen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.9"/> hæfde ⁊ eft oðswerian<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.11"/> wille, oþswerie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.11"/> be ðam wite ⁊ be ðæs feos<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.9"/> wyrðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.1"/>; gif he þonne oþswerian<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.12"/> nylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.1"/>, gebete ðone mænan að twybote.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.1"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="35.1" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="104" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf mon to ðæm men feoh getéme, þe his ætsworen hæfde ⁊ eft ætswerian wylle, swerig<hi rend="italic">e</hi> be ðam wite ⁊ be ðæs feos wyrðe; gyf he ætswerian nylle, gebete ðone mænan að twygbote.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="35.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="105" ed="#liebermann"/>Si ad illum hominem pecunia<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.17"/> uocetur, qui prius abiurauerat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.18"/> uel abiurare uult<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.19"/>, perneget secundum modum wite et pretium pecunie. Si nolit abiurare, emendet ipsum meanan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.20"/> að (id<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.21"/> est periurium) dupliciter.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="46" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif mon to þam men feoh geteme, ðe his ǽr oðswaren<ptr type="editorNote" n="20" target="#Ine_35-1.attnote.fn.20"/> hæfde ⁊ eft oðswerian<ptr type="editorNote" n="21" target="#Ine_35-1.attnote.fn.21"/> wille, oðswerige<ptr type="editorNote" n="22" target="#Ine_35-1.attnote.fn.22"/> be ðam wite ⁊ be ðæs feos weorðe; gif he<ptr type="editorNote" n="23" target="#Ine_35-1.attnote.fn.23"/> oðswerian<ptr type="editorNote" n="21" target="#Ine_35-1.attnote.fn.21-2"/> nylle, gebete þone mænan að twybote.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="36" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="402" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif mon to þam men feoh geteme ðe his ær oðswaren hæfde, ⁊ eft oðswerian wille, oðswerige be ðam wite ⁊ be ðæs feos weorðe; gif he oðswerian nylle, gebete þone mænan að twybote.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.de.1"/><pb n="105" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn ein Werthstück auf denselben Mann<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.de.2"/> zur Gewähr gezogen wird, der sich davon [schon] früher frei geschworen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.de.3"/> hatte und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.de.4"/> nochmals frei zu schwören bereit ist, so schwöre er sich frei [durch Eid<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.de.5"/>] in Höhe des Strafgeldes und in Höhe des Sachwerthes; wenn er (aber<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.de.6"/>) sich [jetzt davon] nicht losschwören will, büsse er jenen Meineid<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.de.7"/> doppelt.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_35-1.lnote.de.8"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If an item of value is vouched to warranty against the same man who had [already] previously sworn himself free of it and is prepared to swear himself free again, let him swear himself free [by an oath] to the amount of the fine and to the amount of the value of the thing; (but) if he will not swear himself free [of it now], let him pay double for that perjury.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="47" ed="#attenborough"/>If a man is vouched to warranty for livestock and he has previously disowned the transaction and wishes again to disown it, the oath required of him shall be equal to the amount of the fine involved and the value of the stock. If he does not wish to disown the transaction [a second time], he shall pay double compensation<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_35-1.attnote.n.1"/> for his false oath.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="403" ed="#whitelock"/>If one vouches to warranty for property a man who had previously denied it on oath, and wishes to deny it again, he is to deny it with an oath equivalent to the fine and to the value of the property; if he will not deny it on oath, he is to pay double compensation for the false oath.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="403" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If a man is vouched to warranty for property which he earlier has denied on oath [was illegally obtained], and he wishes to deny it on oath again, let him deny it by [an oath in the amount of] the fine and by [an oath in the amount of] the property. If he does not wish to deny it [the second time], let him pay for the false oath two-fold.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="280"><ref target="clause:Af_22">Af 22</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">104</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">105</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in MHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">105</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">adiu. <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">adiu. K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">105</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uelit <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uelit K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_35-1.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">105</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">menen aaþ <hi rend="italic">K;</hi> met nanað <hi rend="italic">T;</hi> mainað <hi rend="italic">MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">menen aaþ K; met nanað T; mainað MHkBr</seg></note>
