        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_35-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hier müsste neues Kapitel beginnen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">A new chapter ought to begin here</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_35-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Meineid 12; Rauch <hi rend="italic">Spurfolge</hi> 30f. Hermann <hi rend="italic">Mobiliarvindikation</hi> 63 meint, Beklagter habe die Sache früher nur zur Leihe besessen: das konnte Ine nicht auslassen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Meineid 12; Rauch <hi rend="italic">Spurfolge</hi> 30f. Hermann <hi rend="italic">Mobiliarvindikation</hi> 63 holds that the defendant had previously possessed the thing only on loan: Ine could not have left that out</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_35-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">B modernisiert <hi rend="italic">oð-</hi> häufig zu <hi rend="italic">æt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">B often modernises <hi rend="italic">oð-</hi> to <hi rend="italic">æt</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_35-1.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">uel</hi> mlat. oft ‘und’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">uel</hi> in Medieval Latin often ‘and’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_35-1.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Eidesschwere 3. Nicht ‘bei Vermeidung der Haftung als Dieb und für Schadenersatz an den belangten Inhaber’, wie Hermann versteht. Das folgende ‘und’ = <hi rend="italic">plus</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Eidesschwere 3. Not ‘on pain of liability as a thief and for compensation to the holder who has been sued’, as Hermann understands it. The following ‘and’ = <hi rend="italic">plus</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_35-1.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zusatz H’s, sinngemäss</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Addition by H, in keeping with the sense</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_35-1.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q verstand anfangs das Wort nicht</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q at first did not understand the word</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_35-1.lnote.de.8" n="8" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Das Wort ‘büssen’ und <hi rend="italic">bot</hi> in <hi rend="italic">twybote</hi> dient oft auch für ‘Strafgeld’. Schmid 631 denkt ans Doppelte der 36 Schill. Strafgeld für den mit Diebstahlware ertappten Kaufmann, Cosack <hi rend="italic">Eidhelfer</hi> 67 ausserdem an die 30 Schill. Strafe für falsch Zeugnis II As 10, 1. Mir scheint 120 Schill., das Doppelte der Diebstahlstrafe, für den Richter gemeint; doppelten Ersatz erhält der Kläger im Anefang; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 23f.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The word ‘compensate’, and <hi rend="italic">bot</hi> in <hi rend="italic">twybote</hi>, often also serve for ‘fine’. Schmid 631 thinks of double the 36 shill. fine for the merchant caught with stolen goods, Cosack <hi rend="italic">Eidhelfer</hi> 67 additionally of the 30 shill. penalty for false witness II As 10, 1. To me it seems that 120 shill., double the fine for theft, is meant, payable to the judge; the plaintiff receives double compensation in the Anefang; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 23f.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_35-1.attnote.fn.20" n="20" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><label>oðswaren</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">his ætsworen</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_35-1.attnote.fn.21" n="21" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><label>oðswerian</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ætswerian</hi>. B.</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The number 21 is printed 2 times on the page (35.1, 35.1), with one footnote.</note></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_35-1.attnote.fn.21-2" n="21" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><label>oðswerian</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ætswerian</hi>. B.</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The number 21 is printed 2 times on the page (35.1, 35.1), with one footnote.</note></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_35-1.attnote.fn.22" n="22" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><label>oðswerige</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">swerige</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_35-1.attnote.fn.23" n="23" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><label>he</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">þonne</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_35-1.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">187</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The amount to be paid is not clear. Liebermann suggests 2 × 60 shillings, Schmid 2 × 36 shillings, others 2 × 30 shillings.</seg></note>
      </div>
